            <ArticleTitle>Short-term angiographic and long-term clinical follow-up of a patient with a malexpanded vein graft stent.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>413-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Optimal stent expansion is considered imperative today in order to prevent subacute stent thrombosis and allows us to minimize antithrombotic therapy. The short-term angiographic and long-term clinical follow-up of a patient with a suboptimally expanded vein graft balloon expandable stent is presented. Intensive antithrombotic treatment along with unimpeded blood flow were probably highly beneficial.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
